  "question": {
    "text": "A particle moves such that its position vector <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> where <math><mi>&#969;</mi></math> is a constant and <math><mi>t</mi></math> is time. Then which of the following statements is true for the velocity <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and acceleration <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> of the particle:"
